{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>Blessed of sons be Asher, blessed.</b> From the mouth of the rest of the <b>sons</b> may he be <b>Asher</b> — and the end of the verse proves it." "<b>And accepted of his brothers.</b> They all bless him. And why? <b>And dip his foot in oil</b> — for his land draws oil like a spring, and all his brothers and their wives anoint themselves with it and delight in it and bless him." "<b>Blessed of sons be Asher.</b> Rashi explained: there is none among all the tribes that was blessed with sons like Asher. That is, its count increased so greatly, the last from the first. And even though Menasheh too increased so greatly, he is speaking of the sons of Jacob." "<b>And accepted of his brothers.</b> When Reuven did that act, Asher went and told the matter to the brothers, and they rebuked him. They said: thus you slander our eldest brother! And they excommunicated Asher. Moses came and lifted his excommunication. Just as they would say to an excommunicated person 'arur' (cursed), so they say to the one who lifts it <b>baruch</b> (blessed). And since an excommunicated person was forbidden in conjugal relations, he said <b>of sons</b>. And since his brothers had distanced him, he said <b>accepted of his brothers</b> — that they should draw him near. And since an excommunicated person was forbidden in anointing, they blessed him <b>and dip his foot in oil.</b> And since an excommunicated person is forbidden in the wearing of a sandal, they blessed him <b>Iron and copper your shoe; your shoe</b> — let them be of iron, and your keys of copper, in the manner of wealth, and with them you lock your affairs, but not in the manner of poverty to lock doors with wooden pegs."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {0 "The wordplay on אשר as both the tribal name and 'happy/blessed' is the implicit argument; the end of the verse ('accepted of his brothers') supports that the blessing comes from them."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:55:35.466369543Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}